"prose": [
{
"from": 129,
"to": 132,
"text": "The block runs: the formatter and the linter; each touched crate's units, then the filtered control entries (each selects only this chunk's new cases: 0 on the untouched tree); the boot test's binary and the drift binary under the `mutants` profile; the host read; the whole unit, integration and e2e layers through the harness; the harness render check; then the operator pass."
},
{
"from": 134,
"to": 138,
"text": "**What is not run, and why:** no round, no live entry and no live start; no mutation run (`inputs#I1`; the survivors' kill is read by the controls below, the next boundary's audit reads the scores); no `cargo deny` entry (no dependency moves; CI's `supply-chain` job runs it). There is no boot-path touchpoint (no start order or `src/main.rs` change); the harness boot smoke runs in the operator pass. Every test start runs under a test-owned home; every new wait is bounded (2 s unit, 8 s for the agents-bound case, `KILL_WAIT` + 1 s for `end_writer`)."
},
{
"from": 140,
"to": 142,
"text": "**The remove-the-guard controls** are implement's one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries; each fired on its own filtered entry, its case named, `--timeout 600`. Each case fails on its own bounded assertion, so a `timeout` reading would NOT read the guard as held."
},
{
"from": 144,
"to": 154,
"text": "| id | File | The edit removes | Case | Entry | |---|---|---|---|---| | `claimed-settle` | `src/run/send/slot.rs` | step 1's settle on the failed snapshot update | `send_a_claimed_session_start_whose_snapshot_write_fails_ends_unconfirmed` | `ctl-root` | | `agents-bound` | `src/run/agents.rs` | the bound: the constant raised to 60 s | `read_logged_kills_a_program_that_outlives_its_bound` | `ctl-root` | | `env-user` | `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/ledger.rs` | `env_names_fault`'s body made `None` | step 5's `Some` case | `ctl-claude` | | `env-empty` | `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/ledger.rs` | `||` → `&&` in its guard | step 5's `user = \"\"` case | `ctl-claude` | | `stamp-shape` | `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/ledger.rs` | `&&` → `||` in `attempted` | step 6's case | `ctl-claude` | | `dot-led` | `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/screen.rs` | `<` → `<=` at `:126` | step 7's case | `ctl-claude` | | `enqueue-wait` | `crates/viola-pty/src/pump.rs` | `>=` → `<` at `:191` | `enqueue_waits_for_room_until_its_deadline` | `ctl-pty` | | `writer-wait` | `crates/viola-pty/src/pump.rs` | the `!` at `:337` | `end_writer_returns_within_its_wait_for_a_writer_that_never_ends` | `ctl-pty` | | `exit-drain` | `crates/viola-pty/src/pump.rs` | the `!` at `:372` | step 11's case | `ctl-pty` |"
},
{
"from": 156,
"to": 157,
"text": "`writer-wait` with its guard removed blocks on `join` until the case releases the writer: the case's helper-thread `recv_timeout` fails first, then the case releases it, so the reading is a failure, never a hang."
},
{
"from": 159,
"to": 160,
"text": "`evidence/remove-the-guard.md`, which the mutants criterion names, has no listed producer: step 16 writes it with the Write tool from the controls' lines, a step outside the block."
}
],
